# excluded/skipped.tflw — CHECK-ONLY FIXTURE (`M154g` step 4a, `C96`): see `named-service.tflw` for
# what this directory is.
#
# Identical in every way to `../kept.tflw` except its directory, which is the only variable `C96`
# is allowed. Under a config with `exclude "excluded"` discovery reports one file; without the
# directive it reports two. And the clause the manifest states out loud — that `exclude` applies
# "when a run names a folder rather than a file" — is the third leg: naming **this file** on the
# command line checks it even under the excluding config.

test "a discoverable file one directory down"
  api GET /health
  expect status equals 200
